{"repositoryId":589085439,"availability":"available","full":"mrmekon/itsy-gitsy","name":"itsy-gitsy","description":"A static site generator for Git repositories","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":79,"forks":3,"created":"2023-01-15T02:00:41Z","updated":"2025-01-15T00:00:30Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://git.trevorbentley.com/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:30.464Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:30.464Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:30.464Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T13:24:30.464Z","stars":79,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A static website generator for Git repositories.","The primary motivation is for self-hosting simple Git repository frontends without a dynamic web application. For self-hosters, there can be many motivations for not wanting dynamically generated content: particularly system resource, security, or maintenance requirements on the web server. Most existing Git repository frontends are dynamic \"forges\" or \"hubs\", where even the lightweight ones are large, complex applications with significant resource requirements and large attack surfaces.","Side benefits include offline, local browsing without a web host, and generation of non-website content. For instance, Itsy-Gitsy is also suitable for generating Git repositories as Gopher or Gemini sites, or even e-mail newsletters."],"features":["Generate static, templated, multi-page output from Git repositories","Index any number of Git repositories","local directories (bare or full)","remote repositories (only unauthenticated HTTPS)","Configurable name, path, branch, description, website, etc."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mrmekon/itsy-gitsy/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"d8c9f1c52400fd8b8527827dbbff783fd69f889e81d9e251b9261f8091c074a2","extractedAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:31.090Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T13:24:31.090